---
// Netlify Forms capture for the pre-launch site.
//
// Nothing is bookable yet, so this isn't a "contact me" form — it's a waitlist
// that doubles as research. The "what's breaking" field is the valuable one:
// free-text from people who self-identified before launch is the cheapest seed
// data for the intake instrument.
//
// Netlify detects forms from the built HTML at deploy time, so this works with
// a static Astro build. Two requirements for that to happen:
//   1. Forms must be ENABLED on the Netlify project (jonmartin-mvp).
//   2. The hidden form-name input below must match the form's name attribute.
//
// The form is named "waitlist"; the radio group is named "interest". Those are
// deliberately different — a field sharing the form's name collides on submit.
//
// Submissions land in Netlify → Project → Forms → waitlist.
---

<section class="notify" id="notify">
	<p class="label kicker">Not bookable yet</p>
	<h2>Tell me when it's ready.</h2>
	<p>
		Both products are being written against a composite company first. Leave your
		email and I'll send you the sample when it's finished — and the price when
		there is one.
	</p>

	<form
		name="waitlist"
		method="POST"
		action="/thanks/"
		data-netlify="true"
		netlify-honeypot="bot-field"
	>
		<input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="waitlist" />
		<p class="hp">
			<label>Leave this empty if you're human: <input name="bot-field" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" /></label>
		</p>

		<div class="row">
			<label for="email">Email</label>
			<input type="email" id="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@company.com" />
		</div>

		<div class="row">
			<label for="company">Company <span class="opt">(optional)</span></label>
			<input type="text" id="company" name="company" autocomplete="organization" />
		</div>

		<fieldset class="row">
			<legend>Which one sounds like you?</legend>
			<label class="radio">
				<input type="radio" name="interest" value="Field Report" />
				<span><strong>Field Report</strong> — something's chronically broken and I want to know what</span>
			</label>
			<label class="radio">
				<input type="radio" name="interest" value="Second Opinion" />
				<span><strong>Second Opinion</strong> — I'm about to sign something large</span>
			</label>
			<label class="radio">
				<input type="radio" name="interest" value="Not sure" checked />
				<span>Not sure yet — just keep me posted</span>
			</label>
		</fieldset>

		<div class="row">
			<label for="whats-breaking">
				What's actually breaking? <span class="opt">(optional — it's the part I read first)</span>
			</label>
			<textarea id="whats-breaking" name="whats-breaking" rows="4"
				placeholder="The hire who can't operate without you. The reports nobody trusts. Whatever it actually is."></textarea>
		</div>

		<button type="submit">Send &rarr;</button>
	</form>
</section>

<style>
	.notify { padding: 3rem 0; }
	.kicker { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--sage); margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
	h2 { font-size: 1.4rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
	.notify > p { margin: 0 0 2rem; }
	form { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.5rem; }
	.row { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem; }
	label, legend { font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: bold; color: var(--charcoal); padding: 0; }
	.opt { font-weight: normal; opacity: 0.65; }
	input[type='email'],
	input[type='text'],
	textarea {
		width: 100%;
		padding: 0.6rem 0.7rem;
		font: inherit;
		font-size: 1rem;
		color: var(--charcoal);
		background: #fffdf9;
		border: 1px solid rgba(46, 42, 38, 0.3);
		border-radius: 2px;
	}
	input:focus-visible,
	textarea:focus-visible {
		outline: 2px solid var(--plum);
		outline-offset: 1px;
		border-color: var(--plum);
	}
	textarea { resize: vertical; line-height: 1.5; }
	fieldset { border: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem; }
	.radio {
		display: flex;
		gap: 0.6rem;
		align-items: flex-start;
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		font-weight: normal;
		line-height: 1.45;
		cursor: pointer;
	}
	.radio input { margin-top: 0.3rem; accent-color: var(--plum); }
	button {
		align-self: flex-start;
		font: inherit;
		font-size: 1rem;
		color: var(--cream);
		background: var(--plum);
		border: none;
		border-radius: 2px;
		padding: 0.7rem 1.5rem;
		cursor: pointer;
	}
	button:hover { background: #3c2a43; }
	button:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--charcoal); outline-offset: 2px; }
	.hp { position: absolute; left: -9999px; }
</style>
